WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.839
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.139 --> 00:00:08.027
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.327 --> 00:00:14.369
Unit four: Food for Thought. In this unit, you will discuss food habits, health and waste.

4
00:00:15.383 --> 00:00:16.489
processed food.

5
00:00:17.189 --> 00:00:22.474
processed food means food changed by industrial methods, often with added salt or sugar.

6
00:00:22.774 --> 00:00:25.203
Too much processed food is bad for your heart.

7
00:00:25.903 --> 00:00:28.985
Your turn. Say: processed food.

8
00:00:31.685 --> 00:00:32.837
processed food.

9
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:34.596
vegan.

10
00:00:35.296 --> 00:00:38.561
vegan means a person who eats no animal products at all.

11
00:00:38.861 --> 00:00:40.988
My cousin became a vegan last year.

12
00:00:41.688 --> 00:00:43.504
Your turn. Say: vegan.

13
00:00:46.204 --> 00:00:47.066
vegan.

14
00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:48.912
food waste.

15
00:00:49.612 --> 00:00:52.610
food waste means food that is thrown away instead of eaten.

16
00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.165
Restaurants produce a lot of food waste.

17
00:00:55.865 --> 00:00:58.296
Your turn. Say: food waste.

18
00:01:00.996 --> 00:01:02.090
food waste.

19
00:01:03.083 --> 00:01:04.305
portion control.

20
00:01:05.005 --> 00:01:07.771
portion control means eating suitable amounts of food.

21
00:01:08.071 --> 00:01:10.779
Portion control is easier with smaller plates.

22
00:01:11.479 --> 00:01:14.363
Your turn. Say: portion control.

23
00:01:17.063 --> 00:01:18.285
portion control.

24
00:01:19.283 --> 00:01:20.250
superfood.

25
00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:24.749
superfood means a food believed to be especially good for your health.

26
00:01:25.049 --> 00:01:27.188
Some people call moringa a superfood.

27
00:01:27.888 --> 00:01:30.470
Your turn. Say: superfood.

28
00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.241
superfood.

29
00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:35.891
craving.

30
00:01:36.591 --> 00:01:39.740
craving means a very strong desire for a particular food.

31
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.330
I had a craving for chocolate all afternoon.

32
00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:45.311
Your turn. Say: craving.

33
00:01:48.011 --> 00:01:48.872
craving.

34
00:01:49.883 --> 00:01:50.815
appetite.

35
00:01:51.515 --> 00:01:53.979
appetite means the feeling of wanting to eat.

36
00:01:54.279 --> 00:01:56.615
Exercise always gives me a big appetite.

37
00:01:57.315 --> 00:01:59.631
Your turn. Say: appetite.

38
00:02:02.331 --> 00:02:03.297
appetite.

39
00:02:04.283 --> 00:02:05.470
locally sourced.

40
00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:09.319
locally sourced means produced or grown near where it is sold.

41
00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:12.164
The café uses locally sourced vegetables.

42
00:02:12.864 --> 00:02:15.923
Your turn. Say: locally sourced.

43
00:02:18.623 --> 00:02:20.030
locally sourced.

44
00:02:21.017 --> 00:02:22.935
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:23.235 --> 00:02:25.710
I've been trying to eat less processed food.

46
00:02:27.017 --> 00:02:28.868
Good idea. How's it going?

47
00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:33.599
Not bad, but I get a craving for sweets every evening!

48
00:02:34.883 --> 00:02:38.418
Try some fruit instead. And pay attention to portion control.

49
00:02:39.717 --> 00:02:42.390
I'm also trying to reduce food waste at home.

50
00:02:43.683 --> 00:02:47.215
Buying locally sourced food in smaller amounts really helps with that.

51
00:02:48.517 --> 00:02:52.118
Grammar focus: Countable and uncountable nouns (advanced).

52
00:02:52.418 --> 00:02:56.577
Use a piece of or a bit of with uncountable nouns like advice and information.

53
00:02:56.877 --> 00:03:01.431
Use a number of with countable nouns, and a great deal of with uncountable nouns.

54
00:03:01.731 --> 00:03:06.610
For example: A number of people are becoming vegan, and we waste a great deal of food.

55
00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:12.927
Some nouns are uncountable in English but countable in other languages: advice, information, news, furniture.

56
00:03:13.917 --> 00:03:16.917
Now read and listen. The True Cost of Food Waste.

57
00:03:17.217 --> 00:03:21.051
Around one third of all food produced in the world is never eaten.

58
00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:26.300
A great deal of this food waste happens in homes, not in shops or farms.

59
00:03:27.617 --> 00:03:30.940
Buying smaller amounts and planning meals can make a big difference.

60
00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:36.606
Locally sourced food usually travels a shorter distance and stays fresh longer.

61
00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:41.855
Small changes in our habits can protect both the planet and our wallets.

62
00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:45.524
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:45.824 --> 00:03:49.147
A very strong desire for a particular food is a blank.

64
00:03:49.447 --> 00:03:52.578
A, craving. B, vegan. C, superfood.

65
00:03:56.583 --> 00:03:58.258
The answer is A: craving.

66
00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.401
Can I give you blank advice?

67
00:04:01.701 --> 00:04:05.738
A, an. B, a piece of. C, a number of.

68
00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.819
The answer is B: a piece of.

69
00:04:13.317 --> 00:04:15.247
blank students have joined the club.

70
00:04:15.547 --> 00:04:18.863
A, A great deal of. B, A number of. C, Much.

71
00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:25.291
The answer is B: A number of.

72
00:04:26.783 --> 00:04:29.085
Food grown near where it is sold is blank.

73
00:04:29.385 --> 00:04:33.317
A, processed. B, locally sourced. C, food waste.

74
00:04:37.317 --> 00:04:39.676
The answer is B: locally sourced.

75
00:04:41.183 --> 00:04:44.054
According to the text, how much food is never eaten?

76
00:04:44.354 --> 00:04:47.972
A, one tenth. B, one third. C, one half.

77
00:04:51.983 --> 00:04:54.053
The answer is B: one third.

78
00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:59.514
Now it's your turn to speak. What changes could people make to eat more healthily?

79
00:05:04.814 --> 00:05:10.866
People could eat less processed food, practise portion control and buy more locally sourced vegetables.

80
00:05:11.166 --> 00:05:12.829
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:13.817 --> 00:05:18.396
Great work today! You learned eight new words and countable and uncountable nouns (advanced).

82
00:05:18.696 --> 00:05:23.020
Today's value is healthy eating. Eat fruit and vegetables to grow strong.

83
00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.578
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

84
00:05:25.878 --> 00:05:28.728
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

